const paragraphs=[
 'The letter arrived with the tide. Mira found it wedged between the door and the stone step, its envelope damp with salt and the address written in a hand she had spent seven years trying to forget.',
 'For a long while she stood in the doorway. Across the harbor, the fishing boats were returning one by one, their hulls dark against the pale morning. Someone was calling a name she could not quite hear.',
 'She turned the envelope over. No seal. No return address. Only a small drawing of a compass, its needle pointing somewhere beyond the edge of the paper.',
 'Her father had always said that an honest map showed its uncertainties. Here, he would write in the margins, we do not yet know. Here, the coastline may have changed.',
 'Inside was a chart of the eastern islands. At first it looked ordinary: the familiar curve of the breakwater, the shallow channel where the ferries passed, the black rocks beyond the lighthouse. Then she saw the new island.',
 'It lay precisely where her father’s ship had vanished.',
 'Mira set the chart on the kitchen table and weighted its corners with cups. The morning light reached across the paper. Along the southern coast, in letters so small she almost missed them, someone had written: Come before the water rises.'
];
